VALUES ('grandmother-names', 'The Grandmother Names — 34 American Names With Almost Nobody Young Left', '34 names have at least 100,000 living bearers and at least nine in ten of them are 50 or older. Every one of the 34 is a girls'' name.', '<p>In 1947, American parents wrote Linda on 99,692 birth certificates. No year before or since produced more Lindas.</p>
<p>An estimated 1,010,533 living Americans carry the name today. Their median age is 72.</p>
<p>Linda is not extinct. It went to 294 girls in 2025. But the children are gone.</p>
<p>We aged every name in the Social Security record through an actuarial life table and measured the living population behind each one. 533 names have at least 100,000 living bearers. Of those, 34 are names where almost nobody is young — at least nine in ten living bearers are fifty or older.</p>
<p>34 names. 10,597,943 living Americans. Not one of them is a boy''s name.</p>
