<p>Susan and Mateo are the same kind of fact. Susan is what America was naming girls when the country was young. Mateo is what it is naming boys now. The record does not rank them. It only counts who got the name, and when.</p>
<p>Every name on the list has its full demographic record — living population, median age, peak year, and the year it last appeared — on its own page. Start with <a href="/name/Linda/">Linda</a>, <a href="/name/Debra/">Debra</a>, <a href="/name/Peggy/">Peggy</a>, or <a href="/name/Dorothy/">Dorothy</a>.</p>', 'published', 'NobodyNamed', '/api/og/default', '2026-10-12T09:00:00.000Z', datetime('now'))
